{title: Wayfaring Stranger}
{artist: Traditional American spiritual}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Spiritual}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: Em}
{key_original: Dm}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I am a [Em]poor wayfaring [Am]stranger
While [Em]traveling through this world of [B7]woe
Yet there's no [Em]sickness, toil, nor [Am]danger
In that [G]bright land to [D]which I [Em]go
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I'm going [G]there to see my [D]Father
I'm going [Em]there no more to [B7]roam
I'm only [Em]going over [Am]Jordan
I'm only [G]going over [D]home [Em]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I know dark [Em]clouds will gather 'round [Am]me
I [Em]know my way is rough and [B7]steep
But golden [Em]fields lie out be[Am]fore me
Where [G]God's re[D]deemed their [Em]vigil keep
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I'll soon be [Em]free from every [Am]trial
This [Em]form will rest beneath the [B7]sod
I'll drop the [Em]cross of self-de[Am]nial
And en[G]ter in my [D]home with [Em]God
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
